Subject: find: on OpenVMS, VMS-syntax starting points and names

A starting point in VMS syntax ("[.tree]", "[]", "DKA0:[X]", "tree.dir")
is converted to a Unix name for the walk, and the names under it are
shown in VMS syntax: [.tree.sub]two.txt, a directory as [.tree]sub.DIR
(vms/vms_names.c; docs/DECISIONS.md D2).  This covers -print, -fprint,
-print0, -fprint0, -ls, -fls, -printf's %p and the {} of -exec and -ok;
-execdir's "./name" becomes "[]name".  A Unix starting point keeps Unix
names, as on Unix.

